    "q-171523": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171523",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The expression $-a-(3a+1)$ can be written as{{field-1}}\n$a\\,-$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we remove the parentheses by distributing the negative sign. This gives\n\n$$\n-a-3a-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we collect like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-a-3a-1 & = \\\\ (-a-3a)-1 & = \\\\ -4a-1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
