    "q-181400": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181400",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The expression $15-3(k+3)$ can be written as{{field-1}}\n$-$\n{{field-2}}\n$k.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the expression we need to subtract from $15$ must be expanded using the distributive law.  \n\nSo first, let's write some big brackets around the expression in parentheses, keeping the minus sign *outside*.\n\n$$\n15-[3(k+3)]\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the expression inside the brackets using the distributive law. This gives\n\n$$\n15-[3k+9].\n$$\n\nNow, we remove the brackets by distributing the negative sign. This gives\n\n$$\n15-3k-9.\n$$\n\nFinally, we collect like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15-3k-9 & = \\\\ (15-9)-3k & = \\\\ 6-3\\,k & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
